nlp_rag_medical.py,nlp_rag_medical.py,62afa897165d7bb9ba172651466707836b388fdf,lcossette1980/nlp_rag_med,https://api.github.com/repositories/982955702/contents/nlp_rag_medical.py?ref=6b19f539e2e956ba20034e170039b2e36fe27a43,https://api.github.com/repositories/982955702/git/blobs/62afa897165d7bb9ba172651466707836b388fdf,https://github.com/lcossette1980/nlp_rag_med/blob/6b19f539e2e956ba20034e170039b2e36fe27a43/nlp_rag_medical.py,,,0,0,0,1,2025-05-13T16:53:49Z,0,0,"# Medical RAG Assistant (Merck Manual)

This project builds a clinical question-answering assistant using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). It leverages LangChain and medical embeddings to extract and serve answers from the Merck Manual.

## 🧠 Features

- Loads and chunks the Merck Manual PDF
- Embeds chunks using SentenceTransformer (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`)
- Stores vectors in ChromaDB for fast retrieval
- Answers medical queries using context-aware LLMs (OpenAI or HuggingFace)
- Evaluates groundedness and clinical relevance of answers

## 📄 Example Questions

- ""What is the protocol for managing sepsis in a critical care unit?""
- ""What are effective treatments for alopecia areata?""
- ""How should you treat a fractured leg while hiking?""

## 🛠️ How to Use

1. Place `medical_diagnosis_manual.pdf` in the `data/` folder
2. Run the pipeline:
```bash
python nlp_rag_medical.py
