minimax.py,langgraph-agent/backend/env/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/chat_models/minimax.py,8320c8fafcb47064f6bb48a75cdaab2a27eac13e,HarianthK/Langgraph-agent-automation,https://api.github.com/repositories/992517894/contents/langgraph-agent/backend/env/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/chat_models/minimax.py?ref=bdba9eb5e1f9553cff1384b3cbe6e4b63a76a2ae,https://api.github.com/repositories/992517894/git/blobs/8320c8fafcb47064f6bb48a75cdaab2a27eac13e,https://github.com/HarianthK/Langgraph-agent-automation/blob/bdba9eb5e1f9553cff1384b3cbe6e4b63a76a2ae/langgraph-agent/backend/env/Lib/site-packages/langchain_community/chat_models/minimax.py,Project for xnode,,0,0,0,5,2025-06-03T21:22:39Z,0,0,"# 🚀 LangGraph Angular Agent for Web Form Automation

This project is the result of a focused, one-day sprint to build a fully functional AI agent platform that integrates data extraction, classification, and automated web form submission — all wrapped in a clean Angular frontend and powered by LangGraph orchestration.

It's far from a toy project. This was built with grit, care, and a lot of late-night debugging.

---

## 🧠 Project Overview

This LangGraph-based AI agent pulls data from:
- 🌐 [API Ninja](https://api-ninjas.com/) — for zip code, location, and demographics
- 🧠 Ollama + Mistral — for NAICS classification and fallback zip/census inference
- 🐘 PostgreSQL — for persistent storage
- 🧪 Selenium — to simulate form submission

And it orchestrates everything through LangGraph to simulate an intelligent business registration bot.

---

