langgraph_to_openai_converter.py,language_model_gateway/gateway/converters/langgraph_to_openai_converter.py,b7f4b2534c27146ab6b5be53b77fbf3907cd91f0,imranq2/language_model_gateway,https://api.github.com/repositories/881110019/contents/language_model_gateway/gateway/converters/langgraph_to_openai_converter.py?ref=879c005ea22988706ff2b78608e554165e21fd41,https://api.github.com/repositories/881110019/git/blobs/b7f4b2534c27146ab6b5be53b77fbf3907cd91f0,https://github.com/imranq2/language_model_gateway/blob/879c005ea22988706ff2b78608e554165e21fd41/language_model_gateway/gateway/converters/langgraph_to_openai_converter.py,Implements an OpenAPI compatible gateway that uses langchain,,0,0,27,451,2025-01-15T22:21:11Z,0,2,"# language_model_gateway

## Overview

This project is a language model gateway that provides an OpenAI compatible API for language models. It is built using FastAPI and GraphQL.
## Prerequisites

- Docker
- Docker Compose
- Make

## Getting Started

To run the project locally, follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository:
    ```sh
    git clone <repository-url>
    cd <repository-directory>
    ```

2. Set up the development environment:
    ```sh
    make devsetup
    ```

3. Start the Docker containers:
    ```sh
    make up
    ```

4. Navigate to the GraphQL endpoint:
    ```
    http://localhost:5050/graphql
    ```

## Example Query

Here is a simple GraphQL query to get providers:

```graphql
query getProviders {
    providers(
        query_id: ""foo""
    ) {
        total_count
        results {
            result_id
        }
    }
}
```

## Running without OAuth
Just run the following commands to run OpenWebUI without OAuth:

```sh
make down; make up; make up-open-webui
```


## Running with OAuth
Since the OpenWebUI uses Keycloak on both server side and browser side, you need to create a host mapping for `keycloak`.

On Macs, this can be done by adding an entry to `/etc/hosts`:

```sh
127.0.0.1   keycloak
```

Then run:
```shell
make down; make up; make up-open-webui-auth
```
